<title>USA: Merrill Lynch Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>Merrill Lynch Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr primary		$1.24		    $1.09</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 1.23		     1.09</p>
<p> Net			481,000		  433,000</p>
<p> Total revs	   8,011,000		6,190,000</p>
<p> Net revs	     3,967,000		3,380,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     379,400		  385,900</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     384,400		  385,900</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTES: Q2 commissions revs $1.08 bln vs $970 million.</p>
<p>Q2 principal transactions revs $1.15 bln vs $908 million.</p>
<p>Q2 investment banking revs $625 million vs $580 million.</p>
<p>Q2 asset management and portfolio service fees $670 million vs $553 million.</p>
<p>SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$2.41		    $2.11</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 2.40		     2.11</p>
<p> Net			947,000		  843,000</p>
<p> Total revs	  15,462,000	     12,209,000</p>
<p> Net revs	     7,808,000		6,641,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     384,200		  388,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     386,800		  389,200</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is Merrill Lynch and Co Inc.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
